@startuml
title Pub-Order Seam Map (integration tests)
left to right direction
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam componentStyle uml2

actor Student
component "React app\n(Login, Menu, Checkout)" as Web
component "Vite dev proxy\n(/api)" as Proxy
component "FastAPI\n(/me, /menu,\n/checkout/review,\n/orders)" as Api
component "Auth check\n(get_current_user)" as AuthCheck
cloud "Supabase Auth" as Auth
database "Postgres\n(menu_items,\norders)" as Db

Student --> Web
Web --> Proxy : <b>S1</b> ✔
Proxy --> Api : <b>S1</b> ✔
Web --> Auth : <b>S2</b> ✔ sign in
Api --> AuthCheck : <b>S3</b> ✔
AuthCheck --> Auth : <b>S3</b> ✔ verify token
Api --> Db : <b>S4</b> ✔ read menu
Api --> Db : <b>S5</b> ✔ write order

legend right
  ✔ tested with real components (local Supabase, no mocks)
  S1 Browser → proxy → API: contract test, full-stack E2E
  S2 Frontend → Supabase Auth: sign-in and full-stack E2E
  S3 API → Supabase Auth: test_supabase_auth.py, rejects guest
  S4 API → database reads: test_local_database.py, SQL checks
  S5 API → database writes: test_orders_database.py (place an order, read the stored rows back), SQL checks
endlegend
@enduml
